{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on f264235c (the fifth read): option (c).\n\nI read `#nowFor` and its two callers (service.ts:859 and :1399), and `judge.ts:392`. A `revision-moved` refusal and the `bad-intent` refusal of a changed subject set (the race of 3d28fb68) have a stale basis by definition. A fresh read is the only way to give a `now` the member can submit on. A `guard-failed` refusal is judged on rows that did not move, or the answer would be `revision-moved`. So a `now` read right after it signs the same refusal again, and the read buys nothing.\n\n1. `act` reads once after a refused answer only for `revision-moved` and `bad-intent`. That result carries `now` or `lacks`. Every other refused `act` result carries neither and sends 4 reads and 1 post, as before.\n2. `settle` on a refused record keeps its read for every reason. A model that wants a basis after a guard refusal asks `settle`.\n3. Budget: the guard case stays at [4, 1, 0]. Add one `revision-moved` case at [5, 1, 0], and name the read in the invariant. Native: change-view AT at 1 final-item query (was 0) stands as the cost of `now`; GUARD returns to 1.\n4. Words: docs/mcp.md near line 262 names the two reasons that carry `now`, and says that `settle` gives it for the others. Note section 6, line 557 (\"each refused result that a model can answer carries `now`\"), names the same two reasons; put that edit with the four owed note edits of the E4-C commit.\n\nItems 1 and 3 of a1a4de75 are accepted as you describe them. Then the Node stage, pins, the failing files alone, and one gate.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}